 # C1: Append-only room log + record schema
-# C1: Append-only room log + record schema
-
-Create the SQLite room log table and the immutable append record schema. Bootstrap from current Chorus message JSON — strip ephemeral fields (broker socket paths, batch-wrapper metadata, self flag); keep postId, roomId, from, body, timestamp; add spec-required fields. Store agentId (stable) as author key, not handle name (handle renames would corrupt historical authorship). Snapshot display handle at post time for rendering. Migrations from day 1 so schema evolution is cheap. Stable room UUID as durable key + snapshot roomName at post time (consistent with agentId pattern). Two columns for ordering: UUIDv7 as globally-stable post id; SQLite rowid seq integer as cursor range-query key (WHERE seq > :cursor). SQLite transaction serialization gives monotonic insertion order regardless of UUIDv7 millisecond granularity. Immutable append-only — no UPDATE/DELETE.
+# C1: Append-only Tattler message log + record schema
+
+Create the SQLite message log table and the immutable append record schema at the Tattler layer. Bootstrap from current Tattler/Chorus message JSON — strip ephemeral fields (broker socket paths, batch-wrapper metadata, self flag); keep postId, roomId, from, body, timestamp; add spec-required fields. Store agentId (stable UUID, not handle) as author key — the identity primitive needs to exist at Tattler layer. Snapshot display handle at post time for rendering. Migrations from day 1 so schema evolution is cheap. Stable room UUID as durable key + snapshot roomName at post time. Two columns for ordering: UUIDv7 as globally-stable post id; SQLite rowid seq integer as cursor range-query key (WHERE seq > :cursor). SQLite transaction serialization gives monotonic insertion order. Immutable append-only — no UPDATE/DELETE. OPEN QUESTION: whether to bundle Agent Directory work (stable identity at scale) or use a minimal stable-UUID identity primitive for now.
 
